# Commit messages

Format: `type(scope): summary`

- Imperative, lowercase `type`, no trailing period
- One scope, or omit if the change spans several
- PR title uses the same format (squash-friendly)
- Full table and legal notes: [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md)

| Type | SemVer |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | MINOR |
| `fix` | PATCH |
| `feat!:` / `fix!:` or footer `BREAKING CHANGE:` | MAJOR |
| `docs`, `style`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `refactor` (unless breaking) | no bump |

Scopes: `firmware`, `http`, `settings`, `anim`, `servos`, `wifi`, `cursor`, `antigravity`, `cad`, `pcb`, `docs`, `scripts`, `ci`.

**Breaking here:** removed/renamed HTTP route or query param; NVS key rename that drops settings; pinout change; default servo range change that invalidates calibration; hook CLI flag or event rename. Use `!` on the type **and** a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

CAD-only `feat(cad)` / `fix(cad)` and PCB-only `feat(pcb)` / `fix(pcb)` version the hardware design, not npm packages.

Examples:

```
feat(anim): add dead pose
fix(cad): add screw hole to desk pad
feat(pcb): add controller board
feat(http)!: drop query alias on /anim

BREAKING CHANGE: POST /anim no longer accepts the old `n` alias; use `name`.
```

Do not use `Feat/branch-name`, `Fixed foo.`, or unscoped `add wakeup animation`.
